<title>UK: UK Estates sells property, plans buyback.</title>
<headline>UK Estates sells property, plans buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property group UK Estates Plc said on Friday it had sold a property in Manchester, northwest England, for 16.1 million stg.</p>
<p>The company said it planned to use the proceeds from the sale to reduce borrowing, increase investment and to repurchase up to one quarter of its issued share capital at up to 29 pence per ordinary share and 87 pence per preference share.</p>
</text>
